{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And this is the offering, etc.</b> Thirteen donations are counted here that Israel gave for the Tabernacle, and corresponding to them Ezekiel counted thirteen garments that the Holy One, blessed be He, is destined to clothe Israel with in the future." "<b>Gold and silver and bronze.</b> Corresponding to them there are righteous deeds in the world: that which a person does when he is healthy is accounted to him as gold; when he is ill and gives — it is accounted to him as silver; when he gives after death — it is accounted to him as bronze. Another interpretation: gold corresponds to the kingdom of Babylon, as it is written: ״אנת הוא רישא דדהבא״. Silver corresponds to the kingdom of Persia, as it is written in that kingdom: ״ועשרת אלפים ככר כסף״. Bronze corresponds to the kingdom of Greece, which is inferior to all of them. Red-dyed ram skins correspond to the kingdom of Aram. And afterward: oil for the light, corresponding to the Messiah, of whom it is written: ״ערכתי נר למשיחי״."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:04:01.321766692Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}